.TH MYSTRNCPY 3 "September 2026" "OS Assignment" "Library Functions"
.SH NAME
mystrncpy \- copy a specified number of characters
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include "mystrfunctions.h"
.PP
.B int mystrncpy(char *dest, const char *src, int n);
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mystrncpy
copies up to
.I n
characters from the string pointed to by
.I src
to the buffer pointed to by
.I dest.
The function returns the number of characters processed.
